The GIVE IAM estimates the social cost of carbon (SCC) with four damage sectors \autocite{rennert_comprehensive_2022}. We add a fifth damage sector for fire PM2.5 mortality. We parameterize key relationships to define a GIVE damage function identifying how fire PM2.5 mortality changes with global mean temperature (GMT) change. 

Key parameters include 1) the relationship between GMT change and country-level average fire PM2.5 exposure per person and 2) relationship between PM2.5 exposure and mortality. We estimate the first while using an existing study for the second. 

